@baseUrl = http://localhost:4002
@conversationId = replace-with-the-id-from-start
@visitorToken = replace-with-the-token-from-start

### What the widget can offer, and the sources it accepts
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/widget

### Open a conversation (201 with id and token). Five per 15 minutes per address, then 429
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/widget/conversations
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Sam Visitor","email":"sam@example.com","message":"I have a question about pricing.","source":"Website","origin":"https://example.com/pricing"}

### A source outside Widget:Sources: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/widget/conversations
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Sam Visitor","email":"sam@example.com","message":"I have a question about pricing.","source":"Elsewhere"}

### A message under 10 characters: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/widget/conversations
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Sam","email":"sam@example.com","message":"Hi"}

### The visitor reads their own thread (200). A wrong token is 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/widget/conversations/{{conversationId}}/session
Content-Type: application/json

{"token":"{{visitorToken}}"}

### The visitor writes again (201). 409 once staff resolved it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/widget/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{"token":"{{visitorToken}}","body":"Any update?"}

### File a bug report (201). 503 while no repository is connected
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/widget/issues
Content-Type: application/json

{"category":"Bug","title":"Example issue","message":"A reproducible problem.","email":"visitor@example.com","source":"Website","origin":"https://example.com/checkout"}

### An unknown category or a short title: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/widget/issues
Content-Type: application/json

{"category":"Question","title":"Hi","message":"Too short."}
